)$ defined over a set $S,$ the $n$th raw moment of $X$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[{X}^{n}]={\\int }_{S}{x}^{n}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, we compute the fifth raw moment of $X$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{5}] & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{x}^{5}\\cdot \\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{1}^{2}{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\,{x}^{4}\\,{|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(16-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f7aca109-b18a-57b5-90ec-bf719ba83078"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f7aca109-b18a-57b5-90ec-bf719ba83078" :answer-field/id #uuid "f7aca109-b18a-57b5-90ec-bf719ba83078" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-99ed83c0-56e7-5eae-a55b-c24cc9289617" :answer-field/choices ["answer-208a0b10-d20c-5680-b78b-191ae08c910b" "answer-92ac3001-cb5a-5ac0-aae9-33678855783b" "answer-dc3014be-44fd-57b1-b8a4-3fe31cb19de9" "answer-99ed83c0-56e7-5eae-a55b-c24cc9289617" "answer-fa2e1283-3791-58ca-a36b-00de002d3091"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-208a0b10-d20c-5680-b78b-191ae08c910b" :answer/id #uuid "208a0b10-d20c-5680-b78b-191ae08c910b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-92ac3001-cb5a-5ac0-aae9-33678855783b" :answer/id #uuid "92ac3001-cb5a-5ac0-aae9-33678855783b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dc3014be-44fd-57b1-b8a4-3fe31cb19de9" :answer/id #uuid "dc3014be-44fd-57b1-b8a4-3fe31cb19de9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{11}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-99ed83c0-56e7-5eae-a55b-c24cc9289617" :answer/id #uuid "99ed83c0-56e7-5eae-a55b-c24cc9289617" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{15}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fa2e1283-3791-58ca-a36b-00de002d3091" :answer/id #uuid "fa2e1283-3791-58ca-a36b-00de002d3091" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186157604 :question/problem "A continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function \n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{{x}^{4}}, & 1<x\\le 2 \\\\ \\frac{4}{3{x}^{3}}, & 2\\le x<4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate $\\text{E}[{X}^{4}].$" :question/worked-solution "For a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ the $n$th raw moment of $X$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[{X}^{n}]={\\int }_{S}{x}^{n}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, we compute the fourth raw moment of $X$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{4}] & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}{x}^{4}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{x}^{4}\\cdot \\frac{3}{{x}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{2}^{4}{x}^{4}\\cdot \\frac{4}{3{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x+\\frac{4}{3}{\\int }_{2}^{4}x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3x\\,{|}_{1}^{2}+{\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{2}|}_{2}^{4} \\\\  & =3(2-1)+\\frac{2}{3}(16-4) \\\\  & =3+8 \\\\  & =11\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186153868 :answer-field/correct 17592186153871 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "question-90065876-8b39-51cd-875c-5aa5721dc0eb" :question/id #uuid "90065876-8b39-51cd-875c-5aa5721dc0eb" :question/math-academy-id "q-131143" :question/problem "Given that $X$ is a continuous random variable with the following probability density function, compute $\\text{E}[2{X}^{2}-5].$\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{1}{3},\\,0<x<3\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we simplify using the properties of expected value:\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[2{X}^{2}-5]=2\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-5\n$$\n\nFor a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ the $n$th raw moment of $X$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[{X}^{n}]={\\int }_{S}{x}^{n}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, we compute the second raw moment of $X$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={\\int }_{S}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{{x}^{3}}{9}\\,|}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]=3$ into the simplified expression, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[2{X}^{2}-5] & =2\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-5 \\\\  & =2\\cdot 3-5 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-dea27d55-adba-575a-832b-07b425bd7bd8"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-dea27d55-adba-575a-832b-07b425bd7bd8" :answer-field/id #uuid "dea27d55-adba-575a-832b-07b425bd7bd8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-ca2112a6-93fa-5273-9274-f2059365dc8f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-3b15167c-cc7e-5c97-9101-4beaf41df4c2" "answer-fd4b8c9f-2f56-5d9d-9eb5-3c123022c710" "answer-5871acd5-eca9-59af-9564-3f4745f98b8e" "answer-ca2112a6-93fa-5273-9274-f2059365dc8f" "answer-c36cdb5e-f036-5f06-b3d4-eee0c3b0cd8a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3b15167c-cc7e-5c97-9101-4beaf41df4c2" :answer/id #uuid "3b15167c-cc7e-5c97-9101-4beaf41df4c2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fd4b8c9f-2f56-5d9d-9eb5-3c123022c710" :answer/id #uuid "fd4b8c9f-2f56-5d9d-9eb5-3c123022c710" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5871acd5-eca9-59af-9564-3f4745f98b8e" :answer/id #uuid "5871acd5-eca9-59af-9564-3f4745f98b8e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ca2112a6-93fa-5273-9274-f2059365dc8f" :answer/id #uuid "ca2112a6-93fa-5273-9274-f2059365dc8f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c36cdb5e-f036-5f06-b3d4-eee0c3b0cd8a" :answer/id #uuid "c36cdb5e-f036-5f06-b3d4-eee0c3b0cd8a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-993709fe-5242-5062-93c5-df6c430c3cdf" :question/id #uuid "993709fe-5242-5062-93c5-df6c430c3cdf" :question/math-academy-id "q-131152" :question/problem "The continuous random variable $X$ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}},\\,1<x<2\n$$\n\nGiven that $\\text{E}[X]=2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2,$ compute $\\text{E}[2X-5{X}^{2}].$\n\n*Hint: You may assume that $\\text{E}[aX+bY]=a\\text{E}[X]+b\\text{E}[Y]$ for any random variables $X$ and $Y$ and constants $a$ and $b.$*" :question/worked-solution "First, we simplify using the hint and the properties of expected value:\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[2X-5{X}^{2}]=2\\text{E}[X]-5\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]\n$$\n\nFor a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ the $n$th raw moment of $X$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[{X}^{n}]={\\int }_{S}{x}^{n}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe already know $\\text{E}[X].$ So, we compute the second raw moment of $X$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={\\int }_{S}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}2\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2x\\,{|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $\\text{E}[X]=2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2$ and $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]=2$ into the simplified expression, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[2X-5{X}^{2}] & =2\\text{E}[X]-5\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] \\\\  & =2\\cdot 2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-5\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-10.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-802be14b-ba00-571d-9732-af1b4692f20a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-802be14b-ba00-571d-9732-af1b4692f20a" :answer-field/id #uuid "802be14b-ba00-571d-9732-af1b4692f20a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-2fa99956-5688-5c52-8334-d71d3728db7c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-aa8387ce-7fb7-5149-8880-aa33c2402f61" "answer-4c69f0cd-2d3b-5d9b-93f3-eb5246d17118" "answer-00ec450b-8c39-502c-a433-fd5a4ae4c4b0" "answer-2fa99956-5688-5c52-8334-d71d3728db7c" "answer-6a512d3a-69fb-533d-ab31-f86e2b7a5a1c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-aa8387ce-7fb7-5149-8880-aa33c2402f61" :answer/id #uuid "aa8387ce-7fb7-5149-8880-aa33c2402f61" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4c69f0cd-2d3b-5d9b-93f3-eb5246d17118" :answer/id #uuid "4c69f0cd-2d3b-5d9b-93f3-eb5246d17118" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-00ec450b-8c39-502c-a433-fd5a4ae4c4b0" :answer/id #uuid "00ec450b-8c39-502c-a433-fd5a4ae4c4b0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-5(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2fa99956-5688-5c52-8334-d71d3728db7c" :answer/id #uuid "2fa99956-5688-5c52-8334-d71d3728db7c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6a512d3a-69fb-533d-ab31-f86e2b7a5a1c" :answer/id #uuid "6a512d3a-69fb-533d-ab31-f86e2b7a5a1c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-8ee689ae-d309-5b9e-a1ff-6e4de3b135ae" :question/id #uuid "8ee689ae-d309-5b9e-a1ff-6e4de3b135ae" :question/math-academy-id "q-90454" :question/problem "The continuous random variable $X$ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=4{x}^{3},\\,0<x<1\n$$\n\nGiven that $\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{4}{5},$ compute $\\text{E}[9{X}^{2}+X].$\n\n*Hint: You may assume that $\\text{E}[aX+bY]=a\\text{E}[X]+b\\text{E}[Y]$ for any random variables $X$ and $Y$ and constants $a$ and $b.$*" :question/worked-solution "First, we simplify using the hint and the properties of expected value:\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[9{X}^{2}+X]=9\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]+\\text{E}[X]\n$$\n\nFor a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ the $n$th raw moment of $X$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[{X}^{n}]={\\int }_{S}{x}^{n}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe already know $\\text{E}[X].$ So, we compute the second raw moment of $X$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={\\int }_{S}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}\\cdot 4{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}4{x}^{5}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{2{x}^{6}}{3}\\,|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{4}{5}$ and $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]=\\frac{2}{3}$ into the simplified expression, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[9{X}^{2}+X] & =9\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]+\\text{E}[X] \\\\  & =9\\cdot \\frac{2}{3}+\\frac{4}{5} \\\\  & =6+\\frac{4}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{34}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-e96a4559-67f7-531f-8a30-e313c843c74b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e96a4559-67f7-531f-8a30-e313c843c74b" :answer-field/id #uuid "e96a4559-67f7-531f-8a30-e313c843c74b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-6292f7a0-9113-56c4-bf5e-7d9b507cd720" :answer-field/choices ["answer-dcac4ef3-4b4f-5d57-a295-5bf2a30e3678" "answer-09fdd550-bf28-5f33-af90-7628e13259a1" "answer-65b5937c-cc39-5723-8f34-9662e8a75710" "answer-6292f7a0-9113-56c4-bf5e-7d9b507cd720" "answer-4965166b-8ac3-5114-9933-f4b87cef16a0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dcac4ef3-4b4f-5d57-a295-5bf2a30e3678" :answer/id #uuid "dcac4ef3-4b4f-5d57-a295-5bf2a30e3678" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-09fdd550-bf28-5f33-af90-7628e13259a1" :answer/id #uuid "09fdd550-bf28-5f33-af90-7628e13259a1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{29}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-65b5937c-cc39-5723-8f34-9662e8a75710" :answer/id #uuid "65b5937c-cc39-5723-8f34-9662e8a75710" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6292f7a0-9113-56c4-bf5e-7d9b507cd720" :answer/id #uuid "6292f7a0-9113-56c4-bf5e-7d9b507cd720" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{34}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4965166b-8ac3-5114-9933-f4b87cef16a0" :answer/id #uuid "4965166b-8ac3-5114-9933-f4b87cef16a0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-78882664-5ca1-5d0e-9798-9cca3f283762" :question/id #uuid "78882664-5ca1-5d0e-9798-9cca3f283762" :question/math-academy-id "q-90451" :question/problem "Given that $X$ is a continuous random variable with the following probability density function, compute $\\text{E}[2{X}^{2}+1].$\n\n$$\nf(x)=1-\\frac{x}{4},\\,1<x<3\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we simplify using the properties of expected value:\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[2{X}^{2}+1]=2\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]+1\n$$\n\nFor a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ the $n$th raw moment of $X$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[{X}^{n}]={\\int }_{S}{x}^{n}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, we compute the second raw moment of $X$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={\\int }_{S}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}{x}^{2}\\cdot (1-\\frac{x}{4})\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}({x}^{2}-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{4})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}-\\frac{{x}^{4}}{16}){|}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]=\\frac{11}{3}$ into the simplified expression, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[2{X}^{2}+1] & =2\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]+1 \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{11}{3}+1 \\\\  & =\\frac{25}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f6b4cbe3-cc32-52a8-971f-7f0c3bceefa4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f6b4cbe3-cc32-52a8-971f-7f0c3bceefa4" :answer-field/id #uuid "f6b4cbe3-cc32-52a8-971f-7f0c3bceefa4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-77000447-b172-5a27-893e-242b163e73c6" :answer-field/choices ["answer-74e3075a-1274-50d8-ab79-2b4f0107f9ab" "answer-beabf677-3eb3-5105-9807-95dfda90570d" "answer-524c0c3b-a863-56ca-980e-5d3036687f18" "answer-77000447-b172-5a27-893e-242b163e73c6" "answer-bde31011-f760-5b4d-85f3-daf008a1415f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-74e3075a-1274-50d8-ab79-2b4f0107f9ab" :answer/id #uuid "74e3075a-1274-50d8-ab79-2b4f0107f9ab" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{19}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-beabf677-3eb3-5105-9807-95dfda90570d" :answer/id #uuid "beabf677-3eb3-5105-9807-95dfda90570d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{20}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-524c0c3b-a863-56ca-980e-5d3036687f18" :answer/id #uuid "524c0c3b-a863-56ca-980e-5d3036687f18" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{21}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-77000447-b172-5a27-893e-242b163e73c6" :answer/id #uuid "77000447-b172-5a27-893e-242b163e73c6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{25}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bde31011-f760-5b4d-85f3-daf008a1415f" :answer/id #uuid "bde31011-f760-5b4d-85f3-daf008a1415f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{9}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-63bcffd8-dbf0-5c48-8ca6-56531c05d1c3" :question/id #uuid "63bcffd8-dbf0-5c48-8ca6-56531c05d1c3" :question/math-academy-id "q-131141" :question/problem "The continuous random variable $X$ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{1}{2x},\\,{e}^{-2}<x<1\n$$\n\nGiven that $\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{2{e}^{2}},$ compute $\\text{E}[4{X}^{2}-2X].$\n\n*Hint: You may assume that $\\text{E}[aX+bY]=a\\text{E}[X]+b\\text{E}[Y]$ for any random variables $X$ and $Y$ and constants $a$ and $b.$*" :question/worked-solution "First, we simplify using the hint and the properties of expected value:\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[4{X}^{2}-2X]=4\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-2\\text{E}[X]\n$$\n\nFor a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ the $n$th raw moment of $X$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[{X}^{n}]={\\int }_{S}{x}^{n}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe already know $\\text{E}[X].$ So, we compute the second raw moment of $X$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={\\int }_{S}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{{e}^{-2}}^{1}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{{e}^{-2}}^{1}\\frac{x}{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}\\,|}_{{e}^{-2}}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}-\\frac{1}{4{e}^{4}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{2{e}^{2}}$ and $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]=\\frac{1}{4}-\\frac{1}{4{e}^{4}}$ into the simplified expression, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[4{X}^{2}-2X] & =4\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-2\\text{E}[X] \\\\  & =4(\\frac{1}{4}-\\frac{1}{4{e}^{4}})-2(\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{2{e}^{2}}) \\\\  & =1-\\frac{1}{{e}^{4}}-1+\\frac{1}{{e}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{e}^{2}}-\\frac{1}{{e}^{4}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-62e8ebaf-8a75-5cb6-8621-5bcf5f7ac9e4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-62e8ebaf-8a75-5cb6-8621-5bcf5f7ac9e4" :answer-field/id #uuid "62e8ebaf-8a75-5cb6-8621-5bcf5f7ac9e4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-33cb4776-7d73-5e89-be66-3abb80c22cd1" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5d5bf664-a18f-566d-a4f7-3bd738b55f2b" "answer-aa2240d8-61b4-5dec-86e4-1ecedc83ab1c" "answer-ce1156f5-fddd-5d6b-adf1-9732ee27312f" "answer-74d74ac0-e401-549d-95e1-5b551db31568" "answer-33cb4776-7d73-5e89-be66-3abb80c22cd1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5d5bf664-a18f-566d-a4f7-3bd738b55f2b" :answer/id #uuid "5d5bf664-a18f-566d-a4f7-3bd738b55f2b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1-\\frac{1}{e}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-aa2240d8-61b4-5dec-86e4-1ecedc83ab1c" :answer/id #uuid "aa2240d8-61b4-5dec-86e4-1ecedc83ab1c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{e}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ce1156f5-fddd-5d6b-adf1-9732ee27312f" :answer/id #uuid "ce1156f5-fddd-5d6b-adf1-9732ee27312f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{e}-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-74d74ac0-e401-549d-95e1-5b551db31568" :answer/id #uuid "74d74ac0-e401-549d-95e1-5b551db31568" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{e}^{2}}+2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-33cb4776-7d73-5e89-be66-3abb80c22cd1" :answer/id #uuid "33cb4776-7d73-5e89-be66-3abb80c22cd1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{e}^{2}}-\\frac{1}{{e}^{4}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186158562 :tutorial/content "Suppose $X$ is a continuous random variable with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S.$\n\nThe values $\\textrm{E}[X]$ and $\\textrm{E}[X^2]$ are called the **first moment** and **second moment** of $X,$ respectively. \n\nRecall that the first moment $\\textrm{E}[X]$ is also called the *expected value* of $X$ and is computed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\textrm{E}[X] = \\int_S x \\cdot f(x) \\,\\textrm{d}x\n$$\n\nTo find second moment $\\textrm{E}[X^2],$ the expected value of the the random variable $X^2,$ we simply substitute $x^2$ for $x$ in the formula above, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\textrm{E}[X^2] = \\int_S x^2 \\cdot f(x) \\,\\textrm{d}x\n$$\n\nLet's compute the second moment $\\textrm{E}[X^2]$ of the continuous random variable $X$ with the probability density function \n\n$$\nf(x) = \\dfrac{3}{2}\\sqrt{x}, \\qquad 0 \\leq x \\leq 1.\n$$\n\nWe compute the expected value of $X^2$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={\\int }_{S}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{3}{2}\\sqrt{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{5/2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}(\\frac{2}{7}{x}^{7/2}){|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}(\\frac{2}{7}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{7}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186158563 :tutorial/content "It's also possible to define higher moments. For example, $\\textrm{E}[X^3]$ is the **third moment** of the random variable $X.$\n\nNotice the pattern:\n\n- $\\displaystyle \\textrm{E}[X] = \\int_S x \\cdot f(x) \\,\\textrm{d}x$ is the *first* moment\n\n- $\\displaystyle \\textrm{E}[X^2] = \\int_S x^2 \\cdot f(x) \\,\\textrm{d}x$ is the *second* moment\n\n- $\\displaystyle \\textrm{E}[X^3] = \\int_S x^3 \\cdot f(x) \\,\\textrm{d}x$ is the *third* moment\n\nand so on. In general, the **$n$th moment** is given by\n\n$$\n\\textrm{E}[X^n] = \\int_S x^n \\cdot f(x) \\,\\textrm{d}x.\n$$\n\nFinally, note that \n\n$$\n\\textrm{E}[X], \\quad \\textrm{E}[X^2], \\quad \\textrm{E}[X^3], \\quad \\ldots\n$$\n\nare sometimes referred to as the first, second, and third **raw moments**. This is because it's possible to define other types of moments.\n\nIn general, $\\textrm{E}[X^n]$ can be called either the $n$th *moment* or $n$th *raw moment*." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186157533 :activity/expected-seconds 600.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
